186:      "decision": "Built the dashboard sidebar nav row from scratch (CAND-020, no prior Figma node) against two Mobbin references: Stripe (default/active/expandable-collapsed rows, no icon-only collapsed sidebar state) and Grok (expanded-parent-with-indented-no-icon-children disclosure). Named, at the user's explicit direction, `Sidebar Menu Row` in Figma (working name during audit was `Nav Item`) with the nested row as a dot-prefixed hidden component `.Sidebar Menu Row Child` (excluded from Figma's Assets/insert panel — nested-only, never inserted standalone) — code mirrors this as `SidebarMenuRow` (primitives tier) with an exported `SidebarMenuRowChild` subcomponent, no separate hiding mechanism needed in code. Design calls made without a prior Figma anchor, resolved this task: (1) active and expanded are mutually exclusive top-level looks (Figma: one `State` variant axis, 5 values default|hover|active|expanded|disabled) — an expanded parent never also renders as active, matching both references (neither showed the two combined); (2) active is colour-only, no background fill (icon+label recolour to `primary`), matching Stripe exactly; (3) hover reuses the existing-but-unconsumed Figma variable `background-hovered` (light `color/neutral/50`, dark `color/neutral/700`) — added to `packages/tokens/atlas.tokens.css`/`.json` and `atlas.figma.tokens.json` this task, the first code consumer; (4) child rows carry no icon and support exactly one nesting level (v1 does not support a second level of disclosure) — matches the Grok reference, which shows only one level; (5) badge/counter composes the existing `Badge` component (`size=\"sm\"`) rather than a new Badge variant — Badge's existing variant/size/appearance set was sufficient; (6) no icon-only collapsed sidebar state — checked Stripe's own collapsed/narrow sidebar via Mobbin and found none exists (sidebar stays icon+label at all widths), so that state was dropped from the matrix entirely rather than guessed. A composed reference frame reproducing both Mobbin sources, plus explicit Light/Dark example frames and a Usage text block, live on the component's own `Sidebar Menu Row` page (not a separate page) — matching the established per-component page convention (see the `Spinner` page: variant grid + Examples — Light + Examples — Dark + Usage, all on one page). An initial draft wrongly put this on its own `Usage & Examples` page; corrected same-session per the user's catch, and that page was deleted.",
